{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Completion-gate remediation for the one evidence-search miss: provider-neutral repair safety is implemented in src/rebar/_commands/_repair_pause.py:1-4 and owned_repair_pause at lines 102-164, which uses refs/reconciler/gate and the leased-lock in-flight probe with no GitHub CLI. Both public repair surfaces route through it at src/rebar/_commands/fsck.py:588 and src/rebar/_commands/doctor.py:227. The executable regression tests/scripts/graph/test_repair_pause_ownership.py:101-117 deliberately intercepts any subprocess argv beginning with gh, runs fsck repair successfully, and asserts gh_calls == []; the same file lines 121-154 proves doctor uses the identical pause contract. docs/release-notes.md:26-37 records the migration from workflow-disable/enable to the durable CAS pause. This is repository-verifiable landed evidence at 694cf894de, not an external attestation."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786428049308831001,"uuid":"dc5f10ba-855d-4767-9524-4ddd379e8811"}